Languages: SDD

Purpose:
  Programming language catalog with metadata for AI-driven technology
  selection. Each language entry provides objective decision criteria,
  not preferences.

Owns: stack\languages.sdd
Catalog:
  Go:
    Pros:
      - Strong concurrency model (goroutines)
      - Simple deployment (single binary)
      - Good performance for I/O-bound workloads
      - Strong standard library
    Cons:
      - Smaller ecosystem than Java/Node
      - Less mature ORM options
      - Steeper learning curve for OOP developers
    BestFor:
      - High-concurrency services
      - Microservices and APIs
      - CLI tools and DevOps utilities
    AvoidWhen:
      - Heavy DOM manipulation required
      - Complex enterprise integration patterns
    Performance:
      - Fast compilation
      - Low memory footprint
      - Excellent for network services
    Ecosystem:
      - Moderate (growing rapidly)
      - Strong in cloud-native space
    Hiring:
      - Moderate availability
      - Strong community support
    Testing:
      - Built-in testing framework
      - Strong table-driven test pattern
    Security:
      - Memory-safe by design
      - Strong typing
    OperationalCost:
      - Low (single binary, minimal runtime)

  Java:
    Pros:
      - Mature enterprise ecosystem
      - Strong typing and tooling
      - Excellent for large teams
      - Battle-tested at scale
    Cons:
      - Higher operational complexity
      - Slower startup time
      - Verbose configuration
    BestFor:
      - Large enterprise systems
      - Complex business logic
      - High-throughput services
    AvoidWhen:
      - Small teams with simple requirements
      - Rapid prototyping
    Performance:
      - Excellent with JIT optimization
      - Higher memory footprint
    Ecosystem:
      - Very large and mature
      - Spring ecosystem dominant
    Hiring:
      - Widely available
    Testing:
      - JUnit ecosystem mature
    Security:
      - Strong security track record
    OperationalCost:
      - Moderate to high

  Kotlin:
    Pros:
      - Interoperable with Java
      - Modern language features
      - Concise syntax
      - Coroutines for async
    Cons:
      - Smaller talent pool
      - Compilation overhead
    BestFor:
      - Android development
      - JVM-based services
      - Gradual Java migration
    AvoidWhen:
      - Standalone services (prefer Go)
    Performance:
      - Comparable to Java
    Ecosystem:
      - Growing rapidly
    Hiring:
      - Limited availability
    Testing:
      - Kotest, JUnit 5
    Security:
      - Null safety by design
    OperationalCost:
      - Similar to Java

  CSharp:
    Pros:
      - Excellent tooling (Visual Studio, Rider)
      - Strong async/await support
      - Good performance
      - Cross-platform with .NET Core
    Cons:
      - Historically Windows-centric
      - Smaller open-source ecosystem
    BestFor:
      - Enterprise services on Azure
      - Cross-platform APIs
      - Game backends
    AvoidWhen:
      - Linux-only environments (prefer Go)
    Performance:
      - Very good with modern runtime
    Ecosystem:
      - Moderate
    Hiring:
      - Moderate availability
    Testing:
      - xUnit, NUnit
    Security:
      - Strong type safety
    OperationalCost:
      - Low with containers

  PHP:
    Pros:
      - Fast development velocity
      - Large ecosystem (Laravel, Symfony)
      - Easy hosting
      - Large talent pool
    Cons:
      - Inconsistent standard library
      - Legacy codebase issues
    BestFor:
      - CRUD-heavy applications
      - Rapid prototyping
      - Content management systems
    AvoidWhen:
      - High-concurrency services
      - Complex domain logic
    Performance:
      - Improved significantly in PHP 8+
    Ecosystem:
      - Very large
    Hiring:
      - Widely available
    Testing:
      - PHPUnit mature
    Security:
      - Improved in recent versions
    OperationalCost:
      - Low

  Python:
    Pros:
      - Fast prototyping
      - Large ecosystem
      - Strong data/ML libraries
      - Easy to read
    Cons:
      - GIL limits concurrency
      - Slower execution
      - Runtime errors
    BestFor:
      - Data processing
      - ML/AI services
      - Scripting and automation
    AvoidWhen:
      - High-throughput APIs
      - Real-time systems
    Performance:
      - Slower than compiled languages
    Ecosystem:
      - Very large
    Hiring:
      - Widely available
    Testing:
      - pytest mature
    Security:
      - Good for data science
    OperationalCost:
      - Low to moderate

  Rust:
    Pros:
      - Memory safety without GC
      - Zero-cost abstractions
      - Excellent performance
      - Strong type system
    Cons:
      - Steep learning curve
      - Longer development time
      - Smaller ecosystem
    BestFor:
      - Performance-critical services
      - Systems programming
      - Security-critical code
    AvoidWhen:
      - Rapid prototyping
      - Small teams with Rust expertise
    Performance:
      - Excellent
    Ecosystem:
      - Growing rapidly
    Hiring:
      - Very limited
    Testing:
      - Built-in testing strong
    Security:
      - Memory-safe by design
    OperationalCost:
      - Low

  TypeScript:
    Pros:
      - JavaScript with types
      - Large ecosystem
      - Excellent tooling
      - Gradual adoption
    Cons:
      - Compilation step
      - Type system complexity
    BestFor:
      - Frontend development
      - Node.js backends
      - Cross-platform code
    AvoidWhen:
      - Simple scripts
    Performance:
      - Runtime same as JS
    Ecosystem:
      - Very large
    Hiring:
      - Widely available
    Testing:
      - Jest, Vitest, Cypress
    Security:
      - Type safety helps
    OperationalCost:
      - Low

  Dart:
    Pros:
      - Flutter ecosystem
      - Good performance
      - Single codebase for mobile/web
    Cons:
      - Smaller ecosystem
      - Limited server-side adoption
    BestFor:
      - Flutter mobile apps
      - Cross-platform UI
    AvoidWhen:
      - Backend services (prefer Go/Node)
    Performance:
      - Good with AOT compilation
    Ecosystem:
      - Moderate
    Hiring:
      - Limited
    Testing:
      - Built-in testing
    Security:
      - Memory-safe
    OperationalCost:
      - Low

  Swift:
    Pros:
      - Memory-safe
      - Excellent performance
      - Native iOS/macOS development
      - Modern language design
    Cons:
      - Apple ecosystem only
      - Limited server-side adoption
    BestFor:
      - iOS/macOS applications
      - Apple platform services
    AvoidWhen:
      - Cross-platform (prefer Flutter/React Native)
    Performance:
      - Excellent
    Ecosystem:
      - Growing on server side
    Hiring:
      - Moderate for Apple platforms
    Testing:
      - XCTest
    Security:
      - Memory-safe
    OperationalCost:
      - Low

TechnologyLifecycle:
  CANDIDATE:
    ?
  EVALUATING:
    ?
  SELECTED:
    ?
  SUPPORTED:
    ?
  DEPRECATED:
    ?
  MIGRATION:
    ?
  RETIRED

